{"id":1,"jsonrpc":"2.0","result":{"capabilities":{"tools":{}},"instructions":"loom holds a falsifiable graph of what this codebase should do, where that lives, and how it is proven. Call loom_status to orient, loom_next for the next correct work, loom_context before editing unfamiliar code. loom records truth it can re-check; it will refuse a claim you cannot anchor.","protocolVersion":"2024-11-05","serverInfo":{"name":"loom","version":"0.26.0"}}}
{"id":2,"jsonrpc":"2.0","result":{"tools":[{"description":"Where this graph stands: the maturity ladder, the compass (the single next move), per-lane queue depths, and code ownership. Call this first in a session and after any change, the way you would read a build status.","inputSchema":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{},"type":"object"},"name":"loom_status"},{"description":"The next correct unit of work, compiled into a prompt contract: the role to adopt, what is allowed and forbidden, the evidence required, the exact write-back, and the files to read first. Omit `lane` to take whatever the compass points at. Every packet carries a packet_id.","inputSchema":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"lane":{"description":"Optional lane to serve from (see loom_status.queues).","enum":["fix","build","coverage","validate","quality","analyze","review","triage","prove","elaborate","ratify","audit","deepen"],"type":"string"}},"type":"object"},"name":"loom_next"},{"description":"Read-only context for an intent, a registered file path, or a free-text query: what the behavior is, where it is grounded, what proves it, which rules govern it, and what has gone stale. Pull this BEFORE editing code you did not write.","inputSchema":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"target":{"description":"Intent id/name/prefix, registered codefile path, or free text.","type":"string"}},"required":["target"],"type":"object"},"name":"loom_context"},{"description":"What a change here could reach: the symbols that transitively call a target,                  nearest first, from the real call graph. Exact and heuristic resolutions are                  reported separately and never blended. Call this BEFORE editing a symbol you                  did not write.","inputSchema":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"depth":{"description":"Call hops to walk back (default 3).","maximum":10,"minimum":1,"type":"integer"},"target":{"description":"A symbol name.","type":"string"}},"required":["target"],"type":"object"},"name":"loom_impact"},{"description":"Run a command loom watches and keep what it saw. Prefix the test command you                  were going to run anyway: the run becomes a re-checkable record over the files                  it covered, and with `for_behavior` it binds to that behavior's proof and is                  graded. loom reports the outcome — you cannot supply one.","inputSchema":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"command":{"description":"argv, unquoted — loom quotes it for the shell.","items":{"type":"string"},"minItems":1,"type":"array"},"for_behavior":{"description":"Intent id/name this run is evidence about.","type":"string"},"timeout":{"description":"Seconds before giving up (default 900). A timeout records as blocked, never as a failure.","type":"integer"}},"required":["command"],"type":"object"},"name":"loom_observe"},{"description":"Read the working tree and return the graph mutations it implies: new symbols in                  owned files, symbols whose callers all belong to one behavior, locators naming                  code that moved, files nothing owns. Observes only — nothing is written, and                  items loom cannot derive say what they need from you.","inputSchema":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{},"type":"object"},"name":"loom_absorb"},{"description":"The append-only record of what happened to this graph: ratifications,                  rejections, observed runs, journey runs, drive turns. Read it to establish what                  actually occurred before changing anything — it is the one plane nothing                  rewrites.","inputSchema":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"event":{"description":"Optional event kind to filter by.","type":"string"},"limit":{"description":"Most recent entries to return (default 20).","minimum":1,"type":"integer"}},"type":"object"},"name":"loom_journal"},{"description":"Apply a batch of graph writes atomically: intents, groundings, relationships,                  verdicts, adjudications, vocabulary, tags. Every item goes through the same                  gates as its CLI equivalent — a batch cannot accept what a single write would                  refuse — and any failure rolls back the whole batch.","inputSchema":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"fragment":{"description":"The apply fragment, same shape as the file `loom apply` reads.","type":"object"}},"required":["fragment"],"type":"object"},"name":"loom_apply"}]}}

